    "definitions": {
      "short": "properly, a cliff (or other lofty or inaccessible place); abstractly, altitude ; figuratively, a refuge ; Misgab , a place in Moab",
      "usage": "defence, high fort (tower), refuge, Misgab.",
      "full": "H4869. misgab I. מִשְׂגַּב noun [ masculine Albr ZAW xvi (1896), 60 ] secure height, retreat ; — ׳מ Psalm +; construct מִשְׂגַּב Isa 25:12 ; suffix מִשְׂגַּבִּי Psa 18:3 +, etc.; — 1. a. = strong-hold, מ ׳מִבְצַר חֹמֹתֶיךָ Isa 25:12 . b. figurative of security Isa 33:16 . 2 figurative of God as refuge Psa 9:10 (twice in verse), 18:3 = 2Sam 22:3 ; Psa 46:8 ; Psalm 46:12; 48:4 ; 59:10 ; 59:17 ; Psalm 59:18; 62:3 ; 62:7 ; 94:22 ; 144:2 . II. מִשְׂגָּב Perhaps proper name, of a location in Moab ; — ׳הַמּ Jer 48:1 (see Schw ZAW viii (1888), 196 Albr l.c .), Αμαθ ; Gf thinks appell. of Kir Moab (see II. קִיר ); most below I. ׳מ 1 .",
